.TH WSH-LAB 1 "" "wsh-lab" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsh-lab \- install and drive sparc guests in Proxmox VE VMs, unattended
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wsh-lab targets
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B wsh-lab media
.RI [ target ]
.RB [ \-\-storage
.IR STORAGE " | " \fB\-\-dir\fR " " DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-checksum ]
.br
.B wsh-lab install
.I target
.B \-\-vmid
.I N
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wsh-lab boot-test
.I target
.B \-\-disk
.I DIR/install\-target.raw
.B \-\-vmid
.I N
.RB [ \-\-keep ]
.br
.B wsh-lab run
.I scenario
.B \-\-out
.I DIR
.RB [ \-\-pve
.IR VMID ]
.RB [ \-\-var
.IR KEY=VALUE " ...]"
.br
.B wsh-lab mirror sync
.I source\-dir
.RB [ \-\-storage
.IR STORAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-prune ]
.RB [ \-\-img\-as
.RB { auto | iso | floppy }]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B wsh-lab mirror link
.I source\-file
.RB [ \-\-storage
.IR STORAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR DIR " | " B\-\-asR " " NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-content
.RB { iso | floppy }]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B wsh-lab mirror list
.RB [ \-\-storage
.IR STORAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B wsh-lab
.RB { serve | ctl | cast }
.RI ...
.br
.B wsh-lab \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wsh-lab
is the sparc lab of the wsh-pve project (lab.py). It watches a guest's serial console and
framebuffer, types on either the way a person would, and records every step with screenshots.
.PP
.B wsh-lab install
creates a VM on the Proxmox VE node it runs on (as root) with a tested profile, checks that the
install media are the tested ones (file name, size and sha256 on the media storage), installs the
target unattended, sets a known root password, writes the marker file
.I /etc/wsh\-lab\-target
in the guest and leaves the VM powered off with its login details in the VM's notes. It never
overwrites an existing VMID. Options include
.BR \-\-storage ", " \-\-media\-storage ", " \-\-bridge ", " \-\-vlan ,
.BR \-\-ip " (an address, or " dhcp " where the target supports it), " \-\-netmask ", " \-\-gateway ,
.BR \-\-dns ", " \-\-domain ,
.BR \-\-disk\-size " (a size the target was tested with: 3G or 9G for Solaris 2.6 and 7), " \-\-data\-disk ,
.BR \-\-hostname ", " \-\-root\-password ", " \-\-user ", " \-\-check ", " \-\-template ", "
.BR \-\-keep\-on\-failure " and " \-\-out ;
.B wsh-lab install \-\-help
lists them all.
.PP
For Solaris 2.6 and 7,
.BI \-\-post\-install " sun26gnu"
adds the SVR4 packages of the owner's own GNU package CD
.RI ( sun26gnu.iso ,
a local medium: not published, not downloaded) after the first boot, with
.B pkgadd \-n
and an admin file, onto the data disk, which
.B \-\-data\-disk
then mounts on
.I /usr/local
(also by itself with
.BR "\-\-data\-mount /usr/local" ).
.B \-\-local\-env
(with it) puts
.I /usr/local/bin
on
.B PATH
in
.I /etc/profile
and the user's
.IR .profile ,
and makes bash the
.B \-\-user
account's login shell; root keeps
.I /sbin/sh
so that it can log in single-user, when the data disk isn't mounted.
.PP
.BI \-\-export " DIR"
(with
.BR \-\-check ,
the target's default install only) copies the disk of an install that passed its check to
.I DIR/install\-<target>.raw
with
.I install\-<target>.json
beside it (date, minutes, package versions), replacing the previous copy only when complete.
.B wsh-lab boot-test
creates a VM with the target's profile from a copy of that disk, boots it, runs the target's
check (login, marker) and destroys the VM
.RB ( \-\-keep " keeps it, stopped)."
.PP
.B wsh-lab targets
lists the catalogue (which targets are automated, their profiles and what was tested);
.B wsh-lab media
checks which targets' media a storage or directory has. A medium is found on a storage by its file
name, or else by its size and sha256 among the storage's volumes (a renamed upload, a mirror link).
.PP
.B wsh-lab mirror
manages a mirror storage: a
.B dir
storage whose
.I template/iso
and
.I template/floppy
hold symlinks to ISO and floppy images elsewhere (a NAS). The folders below the source tree are kept
in the link's name, joined with a double underscore:
.I Solaris/2.6/solaris_2.6_598_sparc.iso
becomes the volume
.IR mirror:iso/Solaris__2.6__solaris_2.6_598_sparc.iso ,
which the web UI shows in the folder
.IR "Solaris / 2.6" .
.B sync
links every
.IR .iso ", " .img ", " .ima " and " .vfd
file below
.I source\-dir
.RI ( .img
up to 2.88 MB is a floppy, larger an ISO, unless
.BR \-\-img\-as ),
skips links that are already right and reports conflicts (exit code 1);
.B \-\-prune
also removes links whose target is gone or outside the tree.
.B link
links one file, named after its path below
.B \-\-root
(default: its file name) or
.BR \-\-as .
.B list
shows the links, their targets and dangling ones (exit code 1 when there is one).
Folder and file names are cleaned as PVE cleans an upload's name (other characters than
.B A\-Z a\-z 0\-9 _ . \-
become one
.BR _ );
a name that contains
.B __
or a folder name that ends in
.B _
is refused, because the link name wouldn't split back into the same folders. The tool only creates,
replaces
.RB ( \-\-force )
and removes symlinks, never a regular file, with absolute targets, and refuses a storage that isn't
of type
.BR dir .
The NAS must be mounted at the same path on every node that runs the VMs; a dangling link hides
the volume, and a VM that uses it doesn't start.
.PP
No install media are included or downloaded: Sun and Oracle software is never part of the project.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/wsh-lab/
the lab (lab.py, install.py, targets.py, ...) and its scenarios
.TP
.I /var/lib/wsh-lab/installs/
the evidence of each install (logs, screenshots, recordings); not removed by
.B apt purge
.SH SECURITY
The installed targets' root password is
.B wshlab
unless
.B \-\-root\-password
is given. It is public (in this manual, the documentation and the VM's notes): change it before a
VM is reachable from anywhere untrusted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wsh-lab-mcp (1),
.BR qm (1),
https://debian.wshosting.no/guides/lab-install/,
https://debian.wshosting.no/reference/mirror/
